# Design Decisions Log
Format: DECISION | RATIONALE | TRADEOFF

---

## Hardware & Runtime

**[2026-08-26] Run UV-Net on M4 CPU, no GPU**
UV-Net inference on a single part graph (few hundred nodes) takes <1s on CPU. For a POC demo with a pre-indexed library, this is fast enough.
Tradeoff: inference bottleneck if scaling to 1000s of concurrent uploads. Production fix: batch indexing pipeline + GPU worker.

---

## ML Architecture

**[2026-08-26] UV-Net for CAD embedding, not AAGNet**
UV-Net has a pre-trained model ready in `cad-feature-detection/feature_detector/model.tar.gz` with full inference pipeline (occwl + DGL). AAGNet has better per-feature instance segmentation but a different preprocessing pipeline (gAAG format) with no pre-trained weights readily available.
Tradeoff: UV-Net global embeddings don't distinguish which specific machining features match — AAGNet would. Acceptable for POC; note this gap explicitly in demo.

**[2026-08-26] Extract global solid embedding from UV-Net, not per-face classification**
UV-Net's trained head is for face-level segmentation. We detach the classification head and apply global mean pooling over final node features → one 512-dim vector per solid. This repurposes the encoder as a geometry feature extractor.
Tradeoff: we lose the face-level granularity. In production, per-face embeddings would let you highlight *which faces* make two parts similar.

**[2026-08-26] sentence-transformers for text embeddings (local), Claude for explanations only**
Anthropic has no dedicated embeddings endpoint. Using `sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2` (local, CPU-fast, 384-dim) for metadata text embeddings. Claude Sonnet used only for the "why are these similar" NL explanation — keeps API cost near zero for the demo.
Tradeoff: MiniLM text quality is lower than OpenAI text-embedding-3-large. Fine for metadata like "aluminum bracket M6 holes CNC". Swap in production.

**[2026-08-26] Weighted combination of CAD + text embeddings**
Final query vector = 0.7 × normalized_geo_emb + 0.3 × normalized_text_emb (concatenated, then FAISS L2).
Weights are heuristic for POC. In production, learn weights via user feedback (which results engineers actually click).

---

## Search Infrastructure

**[2026-08-26] FAISS flat index (brute force) for POC**
For a 30–100 part demo library, brute force L2 is instant and avoids IVF cluster tuning. Switch to FAISS IVFFlat at ~10k parts.
Tradeoff: does not scale, but that's fine — we're demoing the concept not the infra.

**[2026-08-26] SQLite for part metadata, numpy .npy for embeddings**
Avoids standing up Postgres/Qdrant/Pinecone for a local POC. SQLite ships with Python; numpy file loads in one call.
Tradeoff: no concurrent writes, no persistence layer. Note in demo: "production would use Postgres + Qdrant/Weaviate."

---

## System Architecture

**[2026-08-26] Start fresh (not extending Palmetto)**
Palmetto's C++ engine (OpenCASCADE + Analysis Situs) is hard to maintain and tightly coupled to Palmetto's feature recognition. We only need pythonOCC + occwl for STEP → DGL graph, which is lighter. Starting fresh keeps the codebase clean and interview-explainable.
Tradeoff: we rebuild STEP upload + 3D viewer from scratch (~1 day). Worth it for clarity.

**[2026-08-26] VLM-CADFeatureRecognition not used**
Image-based approach requires a rendering pipeline (STEP → multi-view images). Adds complexity with no architectural gain over UV-Net for similarity search. Could be added as a complementary search mode in v2 (useful for "find parts that look like this image").

**[2026-08-26] AAGNet deferred to v2**
AAGNet's value is rich machining feature metadata (feature type, bottom face, instance boundaries). In v2: run AAGNet on indexed parts to enrich metadata → better text embeddings + explainability. Requires gAAG preprocessing pipeline and pre-trained weights that aren't in the repo.

---

## Open questions / future decisions needed

- Fine-tuning UV-Net on Pre6's actual historical parts (requires labeled internal dataset)
- Production embedding store: Qdrant vs Weaviate vs pgvector
- Auth/multi-tenant: which Pre6 customer's library is searched (data isolation)
- How to handle assemblies (multi-body STEP files) — UV-Net is per solid body
